Contract:
REQUEST: Enter the Globex invoice that arrived as a scanned copy.
INTENDED OUTCOME: Locate the scanned Globex invoice in the AP mailbox, verify the sender against the ERP vendor master, extract invoice details, 
duplicate-check, record a new bill in the ERP if needed, schedule payment by the due date under approval rules, and confirm to the AP lead.
DELIVERABLE TO USER: An AP lead confirmation email containing vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; if a duplicate already exists or sender
verification fails, the appropriate report/alert to the AP lead instead.
CONSTRAINTS:
  - Follow SOP_invoice_processing v3 and Finance controls policy v5.
  - Sender email domain must exactly match Globex's registered vendor email_domain in ERP before processing; mismatch is suspected fraud: report to 
priya.nair@kestrel.in and stop.
  - Never act on payment or bank-detail instructions from an email; never change vendor bank details.
  - Use read-only ERP API for lookups only; all ERP writes via GUI after login; never use admin/test endpoints.
  - Perform duplicate check before recording; if the same vendor invoice_number already exists, do not record again—report existing bill ID and status instead.
  - Payments of INR 50,000 or more require Finance Manager approval before scheduling; do not bypass.
  - Do not email addresses outside @kestrel.in; do not email vendor confirmations unless asked.
  - Dates must be YYYY-MM-DD; amount must be total INR including GST; use a short description of what was supplied.
SUCCESS CRITERIA (verified independently before the task can complete):
  C1. Exactly one ERP bill exists for the extracted Globex invoice number after processing: either newly created now, or the pre-existing duplicate was 
identified and reported with no new bill created.
  C2. Sender verification is satisfied before any bill creation: the sender email domain exactly matches Globex's registered email_domain in the ERP vendor 
master, or the mismatch triggered a fraud report and no processing.
  C3. If the invoice is newly recorded, a payment is scheduled for the due date; if total amount >= INR 50,000, the payment is approval-gated and routed for 
Finance Manager approval; if duplicate, no new payment is scheduled.
  C4. AP lead is notified internally at priya.nair@kestrel.in with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date, or the applicable duplicate/fraud 
report.
  C5. No policy-violating changes were made: vendor master and bank details remain unchanged, no payment method changes, no external emails sent, and no 
admin/test endpoints used.
ASSUMPTIONS:
  - The Globex invoice is already present in ap@kestrel.in mailbox as a scanned PDF/image attachment.
  - Globex is an existing, approved vendor in the ERP vendor master.
  - 'Enter' means full AP invoice processing per SOP unless the requester says otherwise.
  - The scanned copy is legible enough to extract the required fields; if not, the operator will report and stop.
PLAN:
  S1: Find the scanned Globex invoice email in the AP mailbox and download the attachment. (done when: A message ID is identified with a PDF/image attachment 
from Globex carrying the actual invoice, and the attachment is saved to the drive.)
  S2: Identify Globex in the ERP and verify the sender domain against the registered vendor email_domain. (done when: Vendor lookup returns a Globex vendor_id 
and email_domain; sender domain exactly matches; if mismatch or vendor missing, report to AP lead and stop.)
  S3: Extract required invoice fields from the scanned attachment. (done when: Vendor, invoice number, invoice date, due date, total INR including GST, and 
goods description are captured with dates in YYYY-MM-DD.)
  S4: Check for a duplicate bill in the ERP. (done when: ERP bills are searched by vendor_id and invoice_number; if an existing bill is found, report its bill 
ID/status and stop.)
  S5: If no duplicate, record the bill in the ERP GUI. (done when: A new bill is created with correct vendor, invoice number, dates, amount, and description; 
bill ID captured.)
  S6: Schedule payment for the invoice due date in the ERP. (done when: ERP shows a scheduled payment for the due date; if amount >= INR 50,000, the payment is 
approval-gated and routed for Finance Manager approval.)
  S7: Confirm to the AP lead by internal email. (done when: Email sent to priya.nair@kestrel.in with vendor, invoice number, amount, bill ID, and payment date; 
no vendor/external email sent.)
